# Synauson End User License Agreement

**Version 1.13**
**Effective date:** October 14, 2026
**Licensor:** Synauson LLC, a Utah limited liability company

This End User License Agreement (the "**Agreement**") is between Synauson LLC
("**Synauson**", "**we**" or "**us**") and the business or other organization that
accepts it ("**Customer**" or "**you**"). It governs your use of the synauson
engine and the related materials described below. If you accept on behalf of an
organization, you confirm that you have authority to bind it. If you accept as an
individual for your own business, "Customer" means you.

The Software is for business and professional use, not personal or household use.

---

## 1. Definitions

Capitalized terms have the meanings below. Other terms are defined where they first
appear.

1.1 "**Affiliate**" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with a party, where "control" means owning more than 50% of the
voting interests or having the power to direct its management.

1.2 "**AI Capability**" means a feature of the Software that uses a Model, such as
voice activity detection, end-of-turn detection, speech-to-text or text-to-speech.

1.3 "**AI Session**" means one participant in a Conference, for as long as that
participant uses one or more AI Capabilities. A participant counts as one AI Session
however many AI Capabilities it uses. Participants that use no AI Capability are not
AI Sessions. A Conference is not an AI Session either: it counts against the
Conference Limit, and each AI Session in it counts against the Session Limit (Section
3.1).

1.4 "**Bonus Sessions**" means the AI Sessions added to your Session Limit under the
Model Improvement Program (Sections 13.6 and 13.7).

1.5 "**Call**" means one participant's connection to a Conference handled by the
Software, from when the participant joins until it leaves.

1.6 "**Conference**" means one conference that an Instance runs, with or without AI
Capabilities and whether or not anyone is connected to it, from its creation until it
ends.

1.7 "**Conference Limit**" means the number of Conferences that may run at the same
time under your License File: the Free Plan's base of 10, plus any Conferences you
buy. Bonus Sessions add nothing to it. Only an Order Form can make the Conference
Limit unlimited. The Conference Limit and the Session Limit are independent, and
both apply (Section 3.1).

1.8 "**Customer Product**" means a product or service that you build and that
incorporates or calls the Software.

1.9 "**Documentation**" means the user and operator documentation Synauson publishes
for the release of the Software you run. A later edit to the Documentation does not
change what that release does or what this Agreement lets you do with it.

1.10 "**End User**" means a third party to whom you distribute the Software as part
of a Customer Product under Section 4.

1.11 "**Engine Libraries**" means the proprietary native libraries Synauson
distributes for use in-process from other software, including the libraries inside
the jsyn-natives packages for each supported platform.

1.12 "**Free Plan**" means the Plan Synauson issues without charge (Section 2.3).

1.13 "**Instance**" means one running copy of the Software: one server process, or
one in-process runtime of the Engine Libraries.

1.14 "**License Data**" means the information the Software sends to the Synauson
Services to renew its License File, report usage and download Models, as Sections
12.3 and 12.4 list it, including Usage Reports.

1.15 "**License File**" means the signed file the Software obtains in exchange for a
License Key, or that Synauson provides for an air-gapped deployment (Section 9.3). It
states your Plan, your Session Limit and your Conference Limit, the date your paid
Plan's subscription ends or your Developer License (Section 2.8) expires, if any, and
the date by which the License File must be renewed.

1.16 "**License Key**" means the key Synauson issues to you to identify your
license.

1.17 "**Model**" means a machine learning model, with its weights, vocabularies,
voices, lexicons and related data files, that the Software downloads or that you
import into its model store. Each Model is identified by a codename and a generation
number, such as "spartito-1".

1.18 "**Model Terms**" means the license terms, notices and attributions that apply
to a Model, as set out in that Model's Notice File.

1.19 "**Model Improvement Program**" or "**Program**" means the optional program in
Section 13, and "**Program Data**" means the statistics Section 13.2 describes.

1.20 "**Notice File**" means a file of third-party notices and license texts that
Synauson provides with the Software or with a Model.

1.21 "**Open-Source Component**" means software, data or other material in or
distributed with the Software that its owner licenses under an Open-Source License.

1.22 "**Open-Source License**" means a license approved by the Open Source
Initiative, a free software license published by the Free Software Foundation, a
Creative Commons license that permits modification and redistribution, or any other
license under which the owner of a component makes it available to the public with
permission to copy, modify and redistribute it.

1.23 "**Order Form**" means an ordering document, quote, statement of work or written
license grant that refers to this Agreement and that both parties sign or otherwise
accept in writing, including by email.

1.24 "**Plan**" means the plan named in your License File. There are no feature
tiers: every Plan includes every AI Capability on every AI Session. Plans differ only
in the number of AI Sessions and Conferences, the burst allowance, support and, for
the Developer Plan, the use it permits and its term (Section 2.8), and paid Plans can
earn Bonus Sessions (Section 13.6). The Free Plan is a base of 4 AI Sessions and 10
Conferences, and a paid Plan includes that base and adds the AI Sessions and
Conferences it buys. A Developer License has limits of its own (Section 2.8).

1.25 "**Separately Licensed Materials**" means the materials described in Section 6.

1.26 "**Server Image**" means the synauson server distributed as an OCI container
image, including the synauson server binary, the Open-Source Components it contains,
and their notices.

1.27 "**Session Limit**" means the number of AI Sessions that may run at the same
time under your License File: the Free Plan's base of 4, plus any AI Sessions you buy
and any Bonus Sessions. Every License File carries every AI Capability. Only an Order
Form can make the Session Limit unlimited.

1.28 "**Software**" means the Server Image, the Engine Libraries, the Documentation,
Synauson Model Changes, and any updates, fixes or new versions of them that Synauson
makes available to you. It does not include the Separately Licensed Materials, the
Open-Source Components (Section 7) or the parts of a Model licensed under its Model
Terms (Section 8).

1.29 "**Synauson Model Changes**" means changes Synauson makes to a Model, including
components it adds or replaces, such as fine-tuning adapters, weights merged from
them and components it trains itself, as identified in that Model's Notice File.

1.30 "**Synauson Services**" means the online services Synauson operates for the
Software: the licensing and usage services, which renew License Files and receive
Usage Reports, and Model distribution.

1.31 "**Usage Report**" means the report Section 3.4 describes.

1.32 "**Your Content**" means the audio, video, text and other data that you or your
callers send to or receive from the Software, and what the Software derives from that
content, including transcripts, synthesized speech, detection results and turn
events. License Data and Program Data are not Your Content.

