## 2. License Grant

2.1 **Grant.** Subject to this Agreement, Synauson grants you a non-exclusive,
non-transferable license, during the term of this Agreement, to install and run any
number of Instances of the Software on systems you control or that a hosting provider
operates for you, and to use the Software for your internal business purposes,
including to operate Customer Products that you provide to others as a hosted
service. You may not sublicense the Software except as Section 4 allows. Your Plan,
Session Limit and Conference Limit set how much you may use the AI Capabilities and
how many Conferences you may run (Section 3).

2.2 **Plans.** Every Plan permits the Software's conferencing and media functions up
to your Conference Limit, with no cap on participants in a Conference, and every AI
Capability up to your Session Limit, in each case while Section 9 allows and, under a
Developer License, only for the uses Section 2.8 permits. While connected, a paid
Plan never gives you less than the Free Plan. The Plans on offer
are described on Synauson's website and in your Order Form, if you have one.

2.3 **Free Plan.** Each organization, or individual acting for their own business,
may hold one Free Plan license. If you hold a paid Plan, its license counts as your
one Free Plan license and already includes the Free Plan's base. Synauson may treat
everyone who requests License Keys with email addresses at the same domain as one
organization, except a public webmail domain such as gmail.com. If an organization
holds more than one Free Plan license, counting a paid Plan's license as one,
Synauson may revoke the extra Free Plan License Keys after at least 30 days' notice
by email (Section 9.8). An organization with a paid Plan keeps its paid Plan's
license. One without may choose, during those 30 days, which Free Plan License Key to
keep; if it does not choose, Synauson keeps the first one it issued to that
organization. You may use the Free Plan in production, for commercial
purposes, without charge and without time limit. It includes every AI Capability for
up to 4 AI Sessions, and up to 10 Conferences, at a time across all your Instances,
with no burst allowance and no Bonus Sessions, and comes without support (Section 11)
or warranty (Section 18). Free Plan License Files renew without charge while this
Agreement is in force, subject to Sections 9.8 and 23.3. Like every Plan, it relies
on the connection of Section 9.2.

2.4 **Paid Plans.** A Plan other than the Free Plan and the Developer Plan is granted
for the subscription term and fees stated in your Order Form or in the purchase flow
through which you obtained your License Key.

2.5 **Affiliates and contractors.** Your Affiliates and contractors may use the
Software on your behalf and for your benefit under your License Key, provided they
comply with this Agreement. You are responsible for them as for yourself.

2.6 **Copies.** You may make the copies of the Software reasonably needed for the use
this Agreement permits, including in container registries, build caches, backups and
disaster-recovery systems. Each copy must keep the Notice Files and the LICENSE file
containing this Agreement that ship with the Software.

2.7 **Reservation of rights.** Synauson reserves all rights not expressly granted in
this Agreement.

2.8 **Developer Licenses.** On request, Synauson issues developer licenses
("**Developer Licenses**") without charge to any organization, or individual acting
for their own business, that has accepted this Agreement, whatever its Plan. A
Developer License is a License Key whose License File names the developer plan (the
"**Developer Plan**").

(a) *Development only.* You may use a Developer License only to develop and test
Customer Products: by your developers and by software agents acting for them; in
continuous integration and automated tests; in staging and quality-assurance
environments; and for demonstrations and pilots, including to prospective customers,
that carry no live traffic. You may not use a Developer License in production,
meaning to handle live Calls for your End Users, your customers or your own business
operations, or any Call from a person who is not testing the Customer Product or
watching a demonstration of it.

(b) *Limits.* Each Developer License has its own Session Limit of 4 AI Sessions and
its own Conference Limit of 10 Conferences, with no burst allowance, no Bonus Sessions
and no fees for use above them. Use under a Developer License never counts against
your Plan's limits, and your Plan never adds to a Developer License's.

(c) *How many, and for how long.* Synauson issues as many Developer Licenses as your
organization reasonably needs, and may ask who uses each one. Each runs for one year
from issue and is renewed for another year on request. A Developer License that
expires does not continue on the Free Plan; Section 9.7 describes what happens.
Developer Licenses do not count as your one Free Plan license (Section 2.3).

(d) *Marking and revocation.* The Software marks a Developer License as such in the
license status it reports and in its logs, and says there that it is not for
production use. Synauson may revoke a Developer License that is used in production
after at least 7 days' notice by email, or one that it reasonably believes is no
longer needed after at least 30 days' notice by email (Section 9.8).

(e) *Otherwise.* Developer Licenses carry the support your Plan includes, if any, and
no warranty (Section 18). Like every Plan, they rely on the connection of Section
9.2, and they send Usage Reports (Section 3.4).

