## 4. Internal Use, Redistribution and OEM Rights

4.1 **Internal use by default.** Unless an Order Form grants redistribution rights,
you may not distribute, sell, lease, lend or otherwise make the Software available to
any third party, other than your Affiliates and contractors under Section 2.5.
Operating a Customer Product as a hosted service, where the Software runs only on
systems you or your hosting provider control, is not a distribution.

4.2 **Redistribution where granted.** If an Order Form grants redistribution or OEM
rights, you may distribute the Software, in object-code form and only as an
integrated part of a Customer Product, to End Users, within any limits the Order Form
states.

4.3 **Flow-down terms.** Before any End User receives the Software, you must bind
that End User to written terms that:

(a) protect Synauson and the Software at least as well as Sections 5, 9.9, 15, 16, 18
and 19;

(b) permit the End User to do everything Section 7.2 permits, and do not restrict any
right that an Open-Source License grants;

(c) pass on the Notice Files unchanged, including each Model's Notice File for any
Model you distribute or that the End User's installation downloads, and require the
End User to comply with the Model Terms;

(d) tell the End User that its installation must connect to the Synauson Services and
will send Synauson License Data (Sections 9.2 and 12.3), and what happens when it
cannot connect or when your License Key lapses or is disabled (Sections 9.4 to 9.8);

(e) disclaim, on Synauson's behalf, all warranties and all liability of Synauson to
the End User, to the extent the law permits; and

(f) make no representation, warranty or commitment on Synauson's behalf.

4.4 **License Keys of End Users.** Unless your Order Form says otherwise, each
installation of a Customer Product runs under a License Key Synauson issued to you
for that purpose, with the Session Limit and Conference Limit your Order Form states
for it (Section 3.1).
You will take reasonable measures to keep End Users from extracting your License Key
and using it outside the Customer Product.

4.5 **Your responsibility.** You are responsible for your Customer Products, your End
Users' compliance with the flow-down terms, support of your End Users, and your own
compliance with the Open-Source Licenses of the components you distribute.

