## 7. Open-Source Components

7.1 **Their own licenses govern.** The Software contains or is used with Open-Source
Components. Each is licensed to you under its own Open-Source License, identified in
the Notice Files and in Appendix A. Where this Agreement conflicts with an
Open-Source License as to the component it covers, the Open-Source License prevails,
and no part of this Agreement limits a right that an Open-Source License grants you.
Code that Synauson derived from an Open-Source Component and changed, where that
component's license allows this, is part of the Software, and the original's notice
and license travel with it in the Notice Files.

7.2 **Permission to modify, debug and replace (LGPL).** Parts of the Software link at
run time with libraries licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version
2.1 or a later version ("**LGPL**"), including GStreamer and GLib. For that reason,
and notwithstanding Section 5 or anything else in this Agreement, Synauson permits
you to:

(a) modify the Software, together with the LGPL libraries it uses, for your own use;

(b) reverse engineer the Software to the extent needed to debug such modifications;
and

(c) replace any LGPL library the Software uses with a modified or different version
that is interface-compatible, and run the Software with it.

These permissions extend to End Users under Section 4.3(b). They cover modification,
debugging and replacement, and do not let you distribute Synauson's proprietary code
beyond Section 4. Your Plan, Session Limit and Conference Limit still set how much
use of the AI Capabilities and how many Conferences you have paid for, whether or not
you modify the Software. Synauson will
not use License Keys, License Files, signature checks or any other means to stop you
from exercising these permissions, and replacing an LGPL library does not by itself
affect your License File.

7.3 **Support and these permissions.** Synauson may ask you to reproduce a problem
with the libraries the Documentation names before investigating further. It will not
otherwise treat your use of Section 7.2 as a reason to refuse support, suspend a
License Key or end this Agreement.

7.4 **Source code.** For each release of the Server Image published with this
Agreement, Synauson publishes a companion source image containing the source of every
component in the Server Image whose license requires source to be made available,
including the operating-system source packages and their patches. Synauson keeps each
source image available for as long as it offers the matching Server Image, and for at
least three years after that. Any written offer in a Notice File is part of that
Notice File and is not limited by this Agreement. Synauson's proprietary source code
is not included.

7.5 **Separate programs in the Server Image.** The Server Image contains an operating
system base and programs licensed under the GNU General Public License and other
Open-Source Licenses. They are separate programs, and you may use, copy, modify and
redistribute them under their own licenses, independently of this Agreement.

7.6 **Components you install.** The Engine Libraries need libraries that you obtain
and install yourself, such as GStreamer. Their licenses are between you and their
licensors. If you install plugins, codecs or other components beyond those the
Documentation names, their license and patent terms are your responsibility.

7.7 **No patent license for codecs.** Synauson grants no license under any
third-party patent, including patents on audio or video codecs or formats.

