## 8. Models

8.1 **Delivery.** The Software downloads the Models from the Synauson Services, using
your License Key. You may also copy Models into a model store yourself, for example
to fill a store ahead of time or for an air-gapped deployment, as the Documentation
describes. Only an Instance running under a valid License Key, or a person entitled
to use that License Key, may download a Model.

8.2 **Model Terms.** Each Model comes with its Model Terms, set out in its Notice
File. Synauson gives you the Notice Files of the Models when it issues your License
Key, and you accept their Model Terms together with this Agreement. Each Notice File
is also delivered with its Model's download and stored beside the Model in the model
store, where the server's `synauson models notices` command prints them. Appendix B
lists the current Models by codename and summarizes their Model Terms.

8.3 **What the Model Terms cover.** The parts of a Model that come from its original
licensor are licensed to you under its Model Terms, not under this Agreement, and
nothing in this Agreement restricts a right the Model Terms grant you. You must
comply with the Model Terms of every Model you use or distribute, including their use
policies, attribution and notice requirements, conditions on redistribution,
indemnities and termination conditions. Some Model Terms contain terms in favor of
the original licensor, such as an indemnity or a duty to follow its use policies;
those terms bind you in favor of that licensor. If a Model's Model Terms end for you,
you must stop using that Model.

8.4 **Synauson Model Changes.** Where a Model includes Synauson Model Changes, they
are part of the Software and licensed under this Agreement, on top of the Model
Terms for the original Model. The original licensor's notices and terms still flow
to you through the Notice File, which also states any terms that bind the changes,
such as terms of data used to make them.

8.5 **Availability.** Synauson may release new Models and new generations of a Model,
and may change which Model provides an AI Capability; each comes with its own Notice
File. Synauson will keep the Models that a supported release of the Software uses
available for download while that release is supported (a release for which Synauson
still publishes security fixes under Section 11.1, on every Plan), and will give at
least 90 days' notice before withdrawing any of them, unless the law, the Model Terms
or a third-party claim requires it sooner. You may keep using copies you already
have, as their Model Terms allow. If Synauson withdraws a Model your paid Plan relies
on and offers no comparable replacement, you may end that Plan and Synauson will
refund the prepaid fees for the rest of its term.

