## 9. License Keys and Staying Connected

9.1 **License Keys are credentials.** Keep your License Keys confidential and secure.
You are responsible for all use of the Software under them. Tell Synauson promptly if
one is lost or exposed; Synauson will issue a replacement under Section 9.8 and may
disable the exposed one.

9.2 **The Software connects to Synauson.** Every Instance, on every Plan including
the Free Plan, needs a connection to the Synauson Services, unless Section 9.3
applies. Each Instance sends Usage Reports (Section 3.4), and at startup and about
once a day the same small encrypted request also renews its License File, so one
connection keeps your license current and your pools shared; without it, Section 9.4
applies. A successful contact is a Usage Report or renewal that the Synauson Services
accept. The Software verifies the License File and every response with public keys
built into the Software, and keeps the License File and, in its state directory, the
latest proof of contact. It also checks that each response is current, so the host's
clock must be accurate to within a few minutes. Section 12.3 lists everything
licensing sends.

9.3 **Air-gapped deployments.** If your systems cannot connect to the Synauson
Services, Synauson offers air-gapped deployments by individual arrangement. Contact
Synauson; a negotiated Order Form then provides a License File for that deployment
and states how its AI Sessions and Conferences are counted. Instances in an
air-gapped deployment never contact the Synauson Services or Synauson's status
service, and download no Models; you copy the Models into their model store yourself
(Section 8.1).

9.4 **When an Instance cannot reach the Synauson Services.** Subject to Section 9.5,
an Instance keeps working, within the share Section 3.5 describes, for 7 days after
its last successful contact with the Synauson Services or, if it has never made a
successful contact, for 7 days after its License File was issued. The Software warns
you every hour from the first hour without contact and logs an error every day from
the third day. After 7 days without contact, on any Plan, Calls in progress continue
to their end, but the Instance accepts no new Calls or Conferences, with or without
AI Capabilities, and cannot restart, until it makes a successful contact again. It
recovers as soon as it does, and the 7 days start again in full. If your systems
cannot connect, see Section 9.3.

9.5 **Outages on Synauson's side.** Synauson runs a status service at
status.synauson.com, separately from the Synauson Services. When the Synauson
Services have an outage, Synauson posts a signed outage notice there when it learns
of the outage, and clears the notice when the outage ends; notices are not yet posted
automatically. An Instance whose Usage Reports fail, other than because the Synauson
Services refuse its License Key, checks for a notice about every 5 minutes while they
keep failing, and, when it keeps a state directory, remembers it across restarts.
While a notice is active, the 7 days under Section 9.4 do not run out for an Instance
that can read the notice and whose clock is within 10 minutes of the correct time.
After the notice is cleared, the 7 days run from the later of the Instance's last
successful contact and the clearing. A License File lasts at least 30 days from its
last renewal, and a notice cannot extend it, so the notice protects an Instance only
until the License File it received at its last successful renewal expires. An
Instance that cannot read the notice, for example because its own network is also
down, recovers in full at its next successful contact (Section 9.4). If Synauson ever
stops operating the Synauson Services for good, it will first make available a
release or License File that lets your Instances keep your paid Plan without them for
the rest of your subscription term, keep the Free Plan without them after that, and
keep each Developer License for the rest of its term.

9.6 **A License File to start.** Unless Section 9.3 applies, an Instance can start
only if it has a valid License File and is within the period Sections 9.4 and 9.5
allow. An Instance with no License File of its own, such as a new Instance or one
restarted without its state directory, must reach the Synauson Services to start,
including during an outage under Section 9.5. Keeping the state directory on
persistent storage, as the Documentation describes, lets a restart go ahead without
the connection.

9.7 **Expiry.** A License File states the date your paid Plan or Developer License
expires. The Software starts warning you at least 14 days before that date. If a paid
Plan's date passes without renewal, your license continues automatically on the Free
Plan: Conferences, AI Sessions and Calls in progress finish, and new AI Sessions and
new Conferences are admitted within the Free Plan's Session Limit and Conference
Limit, including after a restart, while the Instance stays in contact (Section 9.4).
An Instance that is out of contact when your paid Plan expires admits no new AI
Sessions or Conferences from a pool whose limit changed until it reconnects and
receives its Free Plan share of that pool.
Renewing restores your Plan at each Instance's next daily renewal or restart. A
Developer License does not continue on the Free Plan: once it expires, Calls in
progress finish, and the Instances under it start no new Conferences or Calls, with
or without AI Capabilities, including after a restart, until Synauson renews it,
which it does on request (Section 2.8).

9.8 **Suspension.** Synauson suspends or revokes a License Key only (a) when it is
exposed or used by someone not entitled to it, (b) for a material breach, other than
non-payment of fees, that you have not cured within 30 days after written notice
under Section 17.4, (c) when the law requires it, (d) for a Developer License, after
at least 7 days' notice by email if it is used in production, or after at least 30
days' notice by email if Synauson reasonably believes it is no longer needed (Section
2.8(d)), or (e) for Free Plan License Keys beyond one per organization, after at
least 30 days' notice by email (Section 2.3). Synauson will notify you by email
before suspending under (b), and as soon as practicable under (a) or (c), with the
reason, unless the law forbids it. Under (a), Synauson issues you a replacement
License Key at once, unless you shared or misused the exposed one yourself, and keeps
the exposed key working for 7 days so you can switch your Instances over, unless it
is being used to harm you or Synauson. A suspension or revocation takes effect at
each Instance's next renewal (Section 9.2): Calls in progress finish, and from then
on the Instance starts no new Calls and cannot restart under that License Key. This
applies equally to End User installations under that key, subject to any wind-down
your Order Form provides. Unpaid fees never lead to a suspension: if fees more than
30 days overdue remain unpaid 10 days after written notice, Synauson may end the paid
Plan they are for, and your license continues on the Free Plan as on expiry under
Section 9.7. Apart from these cases, a License Key stops renewing only under Section
23.3, when a Developer License expires (Section 9.7), or when this Agreement
terminates (Section 17.5).

9.9 **Keeping licensing intact.** Subject to Section 7.2, you will not (a) forge,
alter or replay a License File, a Usage Report or a response from the Synauson
Services, or otherwise get around the licensing of the Software, in order to obtain
AI Capabilities, AI Sessions or Conferences beyond your Plan, Session Limit and
Conference Limit; (b) access the
Synauson Services other than through the Software (including the Software as modified
under Section 7.2) or as the Documentation describes; or (c) distribute any tool or
patch whose primary purpose is to do either. A network outage, firewall or proxy that
keeps an Instance from reaching the Synauson Services is not circumvention; Sections
9.4 and 9.5 cover it.

