## 12. Data and Privacy

12.1 **How the Software stays licensed.** The Software must connect to the Synauson
Services to renew its License File and report usage (Section 9.2), unless you have an
air-gapped deployment under Section 9.3. Sections 12.3 and 12.4 and, if you join the
Program, Section 13.2 list everything it sends to the Synauson Services and, under
the Program, to Synauson. None of it is Your Content.

12.2 **Your Content stays with you.** The Software processes Your Content on the
systems where you run it. Models run locally. The Software does not send Your Content
to Synauson or to any model provider, other than to a service under Section 12.8 that
you choose to use, and Synauson does not receive, store or use Your Content, except
through such a service or in what you choose to send us, for example with a support
request. Where Your Content goes beyond the Software is decided by you and your
Customer Products.

12.3 **What licensing sends.** To renew the License File and share your pools, the
Software sends the following to the Synauson Services, over an encrypted connection,
and nothing else:

(a) your License Key;

(b) on renewal, and when an Instance starts without a License File, requests to
validate the License Key and to renew the License File;

(c) Usage Reports, each containing only: your license's identifier; a random
identifier that the Instance's process creates when it starts; a sequence number; the
Software's version; whether it runs as the server or the Engine Libraries; the number
of AI Sessions active; the peak number of AI Sessions in each minute not yet
received; the numbers of AI Sessions admitted, refused and admitted above the Session
Limit since the last report Synauson received from that Instance; the share of the AI
Session pool the Instance holds; the number of Conferences active, their peak number
in each minute not yet received, the numbers of Conferences admitted, refused and
admitted above the Conference Limit since that last report, and the share of the
Conference pool the Instance holds; the time the report was sent; and whether the
request also renews the License File or is the last before the Instance stops;

(d) the name and version of the Software; and

(e) what any internet connection necessarily carries, including the public IP address
the request comes from and standard HTTP headers.

The Software reaches the Synauson Services at license.synauson.com and
usage.synauson.com. To check for outage notices under Section 9.5, it also reads
Synauson's status service at status.synauson.com, sending only what Section 12.3(d)
and (e) describe. None of these requests carries a machine fingerprint, hardware
identifier, host name, user name, conference or participant identifiers or content,
or Your Content.

12.4 **What Model downloads send.** To download a Model, the Software sends your
License Key and the identifiers of the Model release and file it needs to the
Synauson Services, with the information in Section 12.3(d) and (e). The Synauson
Services answer with a short-lived signed link to the file in Synauson's storage at
Cloudflare (Section 12.7). The Software follows that link without your License Key,
so the storage receives only the request for that file and the information in Section
12.3(d) and (e). The Software may resume an interrupted download with further
requests of the same kind.

12.5 **Connections you configure.** Apart from Sections 12.3, 12.4 and 13, and the
local events in Section 12.6, the Software connects only to systems you configure,
such as SIP and WebRTC peers and STUN or TURN servers. It uses no STUN or TURN server
unless you configure one. Synauson receives none of that traffic, unless what you
configure is a service under Section 12.8.

12.6 **Local diagnostic events on Windows.** On Windows, the ONNX Runtime library
that ships with the Software writes a few startup events to the operating system's
local event-tracing system before the Software turns off the library's telemetry: the
runtime's version, the start and end of loading its CPU backend, and one event for
each type of GPU or NPU present, with the device's name and driver version. After
that it writes nothing per session or per inference, unless someone on that machine
deliberately starts a trace session that turns those events back on. The Software
sends none of these events anywhere. Whether Windows passes them to its publisher
depends on your Windows diagnostic-data settings.

12.7 **How Synauson uses License Data.** Synauson uses License Data only to issue,
verify, renew, suspend and apply licenses, to share and bill AI Sessions and
Conferences under Section 3, to deliver Models, to secure and operate the Synauson
Services, to prevent abuse, to provide support and billing, and to comply with law.
Synauson does not sell it, does not use it for advertising, and keeps it only as long
as needed for those purposes or as the law requires. Synauson runs its licensing
server itself. Cloudflare, Inc., Synauson's hosting and network provider, carries
requests to that server, runs the usage and status services and stores the Model
files. It processes License Data, and what the Software sends when it reads the
status service, only on Synauson's instructions and for these purposes.

On every Plan, the usage service keeps a record of where each license's Usage Reports
come from: each public IP address from which it accepts a Usage Report for that
license (the address in Section 12.3(e)), kept for an IPv6 address as its /64 network
rather than the full address, the country Cloudflare derives from that address, and
when the address was first and last seen, up to a fixed maximum number of addresses
per license. These records hold no names, email addresses, host names or anything
about your calls. The usage service records nothing else about those requests, and
the Software sends nothing extra for it. Synauson uses these records only to detect
and stop misuse of Free Plan licenses and Developer Licenses, and keeps them on every
Plan so that holding a paid license does not hide such misuse. Each record is deleted
90 days after its address was last seen, unless the law requires Synauson to keep it
longer. Synauson never sells these records, never shares them with anyone for that
recipient's own purposes and never uses them for advertising. Cloudflare holds them
only as Synauson's hosting provider, on its instructions, and Synauson discloses them
otherwise only where the law requires. Separately from these records, Cloudflare
keeps the Synauson Services' request logs, which may include the address, for a few
days, and Synauson's licensing server keeps logs of the requests it receives,
including the requesting IP address, the license and the Software's user agent, for
at most 14 days. An IP address can be personal data under data protection law;
Section 12.9 states Synauson's role for it.

12.8 **No new data without notice, and never Your Content unless you choose.**
Synauson will not release a version of the Software that sends Synauson data beyond
Sections 12.3 and 12.4, other than under the Program, or that sends, under the
Program or otherwise, any item, other than Your Content, that the last paragraph of
Section 12.3 excludes, unless it first describes that data in the Documentation and
in the release notes of that version. No version of the Software, under the Program
or otherwise, will send Synauson Your Content, whatever the Documentation or release
notes say. The one exception is a service, such as a hosted relay or a hosted
feature, that Synauson offers separately from the Synauson Services and that you
choose to use through a setting for that service that the Documentation says sends
Your Content to it. That service handles Your Content under its own terms, which you
accept separately, and the Software sends it only the parts of Your Content it needs
to provide what you chose. Only you, or someone acting for you other than Synauson,
can make that choice; no default setting, preset, sample configuration or
pre-selected option that Synauson supplies makes it for you. The exception never
covers License Data, Usage Reports, License File renewals, status checks, Model
downloads, telemetry, anything sent under the Program, or anything else the Software
sends without that choice. Data for improving Synauson's Models or product is
collected, including through such a service, only under Section 13.

12.9 **Roles under data protection law.** You decide which of Your Content is
processed, and how, and you are responsible for it as controller or the equivalent
role. Except through a service under Section 12.8, whose own terms set out the roles
for it, Synauson does not receive Your Content and so does not process it on your
behalf. To the extent License Data or Program Data are personal data, Synauson
processes them as an independent controller for the purposes in Sections 12.7 and
13.5.

