## 13. Model Improvement Program

13.1 **Off unless you turn it on.** The Program is optional and off by default.
Synauson may offer it in a future version of the Software; this Section sets the
terms on which it will run. The Software sends nothing under the Program unless you
turn it on for your license, as the Documentation describes. Declining it never
reduces your Plan, your Session Limit, your Conference Limit or your support.

13.2 **What is sent.** When the Program is on, the Software sends Synauson Program
Data: aggregate statistics about the Software's own operation, computed on your
systems over a reporting period across all the Calls an Instance handled in it, and
limited to:

(a) histograms of processing latency;

(b) histograms of the confidence scores the Models produce;

(c) turn statistics, such as counts and histograms of turn and pause durations;

(d) counts of error codes;

(e) the hardware class of the host, such as its processor family and instruction-set
level, core count, memory size band and accelerator type; and

(f) the versions of the Software and the Models, the Plan, and your license's
identifier, so that Synauson can credit Bonus Sessions.

13.3 **Never a single call.** The Software sends statistics for a reporting period
only if they cover at least 20 Calls; otherwise it carries them into the next
period. Histogram buckets with fewer than 5 entries are merged or left out.

13.4 **Hard limits.** The Program never sends, and Synauson never collects under it:
audio; transcripts or any other text; synthesized speech; embeddings, voice features
or any other representation of a voice or of speech content; per-call, per-conference
or per-participant records; telephone numbers, SIP or WebRTC addresses or any other
identifier of a caller; or anything else that is Your Content.

13.5 **Transparency and use.** Synauson will publish the exact schema of Program Data
before any version that changes it, and the Software lets you view each payload on
your own systems before it is sent. You grant Synauson a non-exclusive, perpetual,
royalty-free license to use Program Data to improve its Models and the Software,
including their accuracy, latency and hardware support. Synauson does not sell
Program Data, does not use it for advertising, and does not disclose it except to
service providers bound to use it only for those purposes, or in aggregate form that
does not identify you.

13.6 **Bonus Sessions.** While the Program is on for your license, Synauson adds the
number of Bonus Sessions stated in your Plan or Order Form to your Session Limit, at
no charge. Bonus Sessions apply to paid Plans only, not to the Free Plan or Developer
Licenses, and add nothing to your Conference Limit. Synauson
does not reduce any Plan to fund them. Where an Order Form grants an unlimited
Session Limit, Bonus Sessions do not apply.

13.7 **Opting out.** You may turn the Program off at any time, and the Software then
stops sending Program Data. Your Bonus Sessions continue until the later of the end
of your current subscription term and 30 days after you opt out, and Synauson will
tell you by email when they will end. Calls in progress are never ended because Bonus
Sessions end.

13.8 **Delivery problems.** If Program Data stops arriving from a license that has
opted in, for example because of a firewall, Synauson will not withdraw the Bonus
Sessions without first telling you and giving you at least 30 days
to fix the problem or to opt out.

13.9 **Changes to the Program.** Synauson may change or end the Program by giving you
at least 60 days' notice by email. A change may not widen Section 13.2 or narrow
Section 13.3 or 13.4 unless you accept a new version of this Agreement. If the
Program ends, Bonus Sessions end as Section 13.7 provides, counted from the end of
the notice period.

