## 17. Term and Termination

17.1 **Term.** This Agreement starts when you accept it and continues until it is
terminated under this Section.

17.2 **End of a subscription.** When a paid Plan's subscription term ends without
renewal, your license moves to the Free Plan under Section 9.7, and this Agreement
remains in force. Your Order Form may provide a wind-down period, including for End
User installations.

17.3 **Termination by you.** You may terminate this Agreement at any time by
notifying Synauson and stopping use of the Software. Prepaid fees are not refunded,
except under Sections 8.5, 17.4 and 18.2 or your Order Form.

17.4 **Termination for breach.** Either party may terminate this Agreement by written
notice if the other materially breaches it and does not cure the breach within 30
days after written notice describing it. Synauson may terminate on shorter notice
where Section 15 requires it. Synauson never terminates this Agreement or disables a
License Key for unpaid fees; Section 9.8's sentence on unpaid fees sets their only
effect on your license, and Synauson may still collect them. If you terminate for
Synauson's uncured breach, Synauson will refund the prepaid fees for the rest of the
term.

17.5 **Effect of termination.** When this Agreement terminates, your license to the
Software ends, you must stop using the Software and delete it, subject to any
wind-down period in your Order Form, and Synauson may disable your License Keys.
Termination does not affect your obligation to pay fees accrued before termination,
or the rights you have under any Open-Source License, Model Terms or the license of
the Separately Licensed Materials, which continue under their own terms.

17.6 **Survival.** Sections 1, 3.6, 4.3 to 4.5, 5, 7.1, 7.4, 7.5, 8.3, 9.1, 9.9, 10,
12.2, 12.7, 12.9, 13.4, 13.5, 14, 15, 16, 17.5, 17.6 and 18 to 24 survive
termination.

