by publishing a new version alone.

23.3 **Accepting a new version.** Synauson may ask you to accept a new version when
you obtain a new License Key, renew or change your Plan, sign a new Order Form, or
join the Program, and may make that acceptance a condition of them. If you do not
accept, the version you accepted continues to govern until your current subscription
term ends, and renewing your paid Plan after that requires the new version; if you
still do not accept, your license continues on the Free Plan under Section 9.7, and
the rest of this Section applies. The Free Plan has no term: Synauson may ask you to
accept a new version to keep renewing Free Plan License Files, by email at least 30
days before the date from which renewals require it. If you have not accepted by that
date, your Free Plan License Key stops renewing: from each Instance's next renewal
after that date, that Instance starts no new Calls and cannot restart, and Calls in
progress finish. This is the only case, other than those in Section 9.8 and the
expiry of a Developer License (Section 9.7), in which a License Key stops renewing
while this Agreement is in force.

