24.1 **Notices.** Synauson may send you notices by email to the contact address
associated with your License Key or Order Form. Notices that concern all customers
may also be given in the Documentation, but notices under Sections 2.3, 2.8, 3.6,
8.5, 9.8, 11.2, 13 and 23.3 are given by email. You may send notices to Synauson at
the address stated on synauson.com/legal or in your Order Form. Email notices are
effective when sent, unless the sender receives notice of non-delivery.

24.2 **Assignment.** You may not assign this Agreement without Synauson's prior
written consent, except to a successor to all or substantially all of your business
or assets to which it relates, with written notice to Synauson. Synauson may assign
it to an Affiliate or to a successor in a merger, acquisition or sale of all or
substantially all of its assets. Any other attempted assignment is void.

24.3 **Force majeure.** Neither party is liable for a failure or delay caused by
events beyond its reasonable control, other than a failure to pay.

24.4 **U.S. Government users.** The Software is "commercial computer software" and
the Documentation is "commercial computer software documentation" as used in 48
C.F.R. 2.101, 12.212 and 227.7202. U.S. Government users acquire them only with the
rights set out in this Agreement.

24.5 **Independent parties.** The parties are independent contractors. This
Agreement creates no partnership, joint venture, agency or employment relationship.

24.6 **No third-party beneficiaries.** This Agreement creates no rights for any third
party. This does not affect any right a licensor has under its own Open-Source
License or Model Terms.

24.7 **Severability and waiver.** If a court or arbitrator finds any provision
unenforceable, it will be enforced to the maximum extent permissible and the rest of
this Agreement will remain in force. A failure or delay in enforcing a provision is
not a waiver.

24.8 **Entire agreement.** This Agreement, with its appendices, the Model Terms and
any Order Forms, is the entire agreement between the parties about its subject
matter and supersedes all earlier agreements and understandings about it.

24.9 **Electronic signatures and language.** The parties may accept this Agreement
and sign Order Forms electronically and in counterparts. This Agreement is written
in English, and the English version governs.

24.10 **Interpretation.** Headings are for convenience only. "Including" means
"including without limitation".

